the knowledge base module_6_examples includes:

the text of the source program is at "sources/module-6-examples.l4".

a governor is an adult if
    the age of the governor >= 18.

a governor has a disqualifying conviction if
    the convictions of the governor is a list
    and a conviction is in the list
    and it is not the case that the conviction is spent.

the person can be a governor if
    the governor is an adult
    and it is not the case that the governor is bankrupt
    and it is not the case that the governor has a disqualifying conviction.

a purpose is charitable if
    prevention_else_relief_of_poverty is equal to the purpose
    otherwise advancement_of_education is equal to the purpose
    otherwise advancement_of_religion is equal to the purpose
    otherwise advancement_of_health is equal to the purpose
    otherwise advancement_of_animal_welfare is equal to the purpose.

a charity is valid if
    the status of the charity is active
    and it is not the case that
        the purposes of the charity is a list
        and [] is equal to the list
    and the purposes of the charity is a second list
    and for all cases in which
        a purpose is in the second list
        it is the case that
            the purpose is charitable
    and it is not the case that
        the governors of the charity is a third list
        and [] is equal to the third list
    and the governors of the charity is a fourth list
    and for all cases in which
        a governor is in the fourth list
        it is the case that
            the person can be the governor.

